# .dockerignore for the Note web editor's docker build context.
#
# The editor's Dockerfile does:
#
#     COPY ui/package.json ui/package-lock.json ./
#     RUN npm ci
#     COPY ui/ .
#
# The second COPY merges the host tree over /app. If the host's ui/node_modules
# were in the context, Docker COPY would overwrite file by file, so every module
# the host has would win over the modules `npm ci` had just resolved from the
# committed lockfile: the lockfile install would have no effect on the image,
# and the published bundle would be built from whatever is on the build machine.
# Excluding node_modules here is what makes `npm ci` mean something.
#
# .git is excluded because the build takes its commit from the BUILD_COMMIT
# build-arg and never from an in-context .git, and history in a published layer
# is an exfiltration surface.

# --- Dependencies and build output: installed/rebuilt inside the image ---
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/target/

# --- VCS metadata ---
.git/
**/.git/

# --- Key/cert material and provider creds ---
**/*.key
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
**/*.p12
**/*.p8
**/*.mobileprovision
**/google-services.json
**/GoogleService-Info.plist

# --- Local env files ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
